From: AOS maintainers <maintainers@andyl.com>
Subject: [PATCH] stub: keep embedded UKI command lines authoritative

AOS UKIs carry a signed .cmdline section.  Measure but do not append
command-line fragments from PE addons or SMBIOS when that section is present:
both sources can otherwise change init selection before the initrd's userspace
validator is able to run.  Measuring the rejected input preserves PCR 12 as a
denial boundary for sealed state.  EFI LoadOptions already follow the embedded
command-line rule under Secure Boot.

Keep upstream behavior for non-UKI EFI images without an embedded command
line.
---
 src/boot/stub.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/boot/stub.c b/src/boot/stub.c
index 3ac6e917d7..f99d52210a 100644
--- a/src/boot/stub.c
+++ b/src/boot/stub.c
@@ -1267,11 +1267,23 @@ static EFI_STATUS run(EFI_HANDLE image) {
         load_all_addons(image, loaded_image, uname, &cmdline_addons, &dt_addons, &n_dt_addons, &initrd_addons, &n_initrd_addons, &ucode_addons, &n_ucode_addons);
 
-        /* If we have any extra command line to add via PE addons, load them now and append, and measure the
-         * additions together, after the embedded options, but before the smbios ones, so that the order is
-         * reversed from "most hardcoded" to "most dynamic". The global addons are loaded first, and the
-         * image-specific ones later, for the same reason. */
-        cmdline_append_and_measure_addons(cmdline_addons, &cmdline, &parameters_measured);
-        cmdline_append_and_measure_smbios(&cmdline, &parameters_measured);
+        /* An embedded command line is part of the signed UKI identity. Measure addon and SMBIOS input into
+         * PCR 12, but do not let it replace that identity before initrd userspace can validate it. EFI
+         * LoadOptions are already suppressed for this case by settle_command_line() while Secure Boot is
+         * enabled. Images without an embedded command line retain the upstream augmentation behavior. */
+        if (PE_SECTION_VECTOR_IS_SET(sections + UNIFIED_SECTION_CMDLINE)) {
+                _cleanup_free_ char16_t *ignored_cmdline = NULL;
+
+                cmdline_append_and_measure_addons(cmdline_addons, &ignored_cmdline, &parameters_measured);
+                cmdline_append_and_measure_smbios(&ignored_cmdline, &parameters_measured);
+                if (!isempty(ignored_cmdline))
+                        log_warning("Ignoring externally supplied command line because the UKI embeds one.");
+        } else {
+                /* If we have any extra command line to add via PE addons, load them now and append, and
+                 * measure the additions together, before the SMBIOS ones. The global addons are loaded
+                 * first, and the image-specific ones later. */
+                cmdline_append_and_measure_addons(cmdline_addons, &cmdline, &parameters_measured);
+                cmdline_append_and_measure_smbios(&cmdline, &parameters_measured);
+        }
 
         export_common_variables(loaded_image);
         export_stub_variables(loaded_image, profile);
-- 
2.51.0
